A multi-declarator `const` lists each declarator as its own outline line, all sharing the statement's line range, and an exported one keeps `export` on each line.
== args
input/multi-vars.ts
== file input/multi-vars.ts
const alpha = 1, beta = 2;
export const gamma = 3, delta = 4;
== stdout
input/multi-vars.ts (2 lines)
[L1-L1] const alpha
[L1-L1] const beta
[L2-L2] export const gamma
[L2-L2] export const delta
== stderr
== exit 0
